azon.com/about-us"},{"title":"Amazon's AI SVP on why AI's biggest breakthroughs haven't happened yet","url":"https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/innovation-at-amazon/peter-desantis-amazon-ai-vivatech"},{"title":"Amazon opens its AWS Trainium AI chips to every PyTorch developer, no rewrite needed","url":"https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/innovation-at-amazon/torchneuron-pytorch-aws-trainium-chips-ai"},{"title":"AWS-to-Open-Data-Centers-in-Israel - Amazon Press Release","url":"https://press.aboutamazon.com/2021/6/aws-to-open-data-centers-in-israel"}]},"The search didn't return a dedicated Decart blog post. The closest match is a snippet from aboutamazon.com's About Us page, which says Amazon to purchase Decart's AI optimization technology to advance chip and model innovation for customers. It adds that the technology is meant to help Amazon optimize inference and strengthen its custom silicon performance. The page is listed as posted 46 days ago.

The results don't connect Decart to Annapurna Labs directly. Annapurna is Amazon's chip unit, acquired in 2015, and the other results only mention Decart as a customer or startup. One result says startups like Decart, use Trainium to train their models and run workloads. So the framing of an "Annapurna acquisition" of Decart isn't supported by these results. The deal appears to be Amazon buying Decart's technology, and the exact acquiring entity is unconfirmed here.

