            "FORGETMENOT (arXiv:2611.29804, submitted 22 November) collected \"around 3800 multi-turn sessions comprising around 6M tokens across five popular AI agents\" and reports that \"user visible memory reveals substantially less (around 20% on average) attributes than the agents store in practice, exposing a significant transparency gap\".",
            "A \"stealth memory injection\" technique raised the amount of personal and sensitive attributes stored \"by 25% and 15% for Copilot and Claude, respectively\". Memory deletion was unreliable: \"all five agents exhibit non-zero post deletion leakage, including health and self-harm related attributes\". A proof-of-concept disclosure to a third-party email recipient gave Gemini a \"31.9% leakage rate\".",
