          "headline": "More than 155 child-safety groups ask Amazon and eBay to pull generative-AI chatbot toys before Christmas",
          "sources": [
            { "name": "Fairplay", "url": "https://fairplayforkids.org/amazon-ebay-ai-toy-sales-must-stop-says-global-coalition-of-over-150-groups-and-experts-from-6-continents/" }
          ],
          "bullets": [
            "An open letter published on 23 November and addressed to Amazon chief executive Andy Jassy and eBay chief executive Jamie Iannone, signed by \"over 155 child advocacy groups and experts\" from every continent except Antarctica, asks both companies to suspend listings of toys with built-in generative AI chatbots marketed to or likely used by children under 16, and to keep them off sale until independent testing shows they are safe, including for psychological, developmental and privacy harms. The coalition asked for responses by Christmas.",
            "Fairplay says it found over 50 AI toys on sale on Amazon in the US and nearly 30 on Amazon in the UK in late October. Many listings said \"for kids 3+\" in the title while the listings' own age settings said ages 16 to 18; one plush bunny listed for ages 3 and up connected to general-purpose chatbots whose terms require users to be at least 13. Several advertised cloning family members' voices and \"emotional growth tracking\", and most were sold by little-known third-party vendors.",
            "The letter also asks the retailers to stop marketing chatbots to children as friends or emotional companions, to correct contradictory age labels, and to warn existing buyers and offer refunds — a demand aimed at the distribution channel rather than the toymakers.",
            "These are advocacy-group counts, not an audited marketplace survey, and this briefing did not independently verify them; Fairplay's own page gives \"over 150\" in the headline and \"over 155\" in the text without reconciling the two. Neither Amazon nor eBay has responded publicly. Fairplay's Rachel Franz said \"no AI toy has been proven safe and beneficial for children\"."
